# CVE-2026-7210: Critical Python runtime vulnerability.
# Fix only available in Python 3.15.0b2 (pre-release).
# Using a beta CPython in production is not acceptable.
# Risk accepted: monitor python.org for stable 3.15 GA and upgrade at that point.
CVE-2026-7210

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack vulnerability bundled inside pip's own internal
# vendored dependencies (pip/_vendor/msgpack) — not an installed application
# package. Only used internally by pip's HTTP cache during image build; never
# reachable by the running app. Risk accepted: not in the runtime attack surface.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2025-47273: setuptools path traversal, detected via pip's internal vendored
# reference — the actual installed setuptools in site-packages is already 84.0.0
# (patched), satisfying requirements.txt's setuptools>=78.1.1 pin already.
# Risk accepted: not in the runtime attack surface.
CVE-2025-47273
